      "writtenOn": "2025-03-06T03:05:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, it seems better that the request that remains is the *first* one to be added. Otherwise, if the following happens:\n\n1. uid 1 starts wifi tethering\n2. uid 2 starts identical wifi tethering\n\nthen tethering will be started only once in, but when tethering comes up, the request will have uid 2 in it, even though the UID that started tethering was uid 1. In effect, this code will \"not remember who started tethering\".\n\nGiven that this CL is a no-op, might want to fix in another CL.",
